{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792523536,"nonce":"Gw4OTwqqx6EhnhQ43pX6KTJTqfY=","title":"TypeScript: persist checked source projects in shared snapshots","message":"Add an opt-in persistent cache for checked filesystem projects, using Zyntax's existing raw typed-AST snapshot format. A valid warm load must skip OXC parsing and frontend type checking while retaining the same shared linker, static release analysis, initializers, array specialization and interpreter-first tiering.\n\nValidate canonical entry identity, every checked source including type-only dependencies, all recorded resolution edges, soundness options and frontend/shared serialization/compiler/target build identity. Re-resolve edges so new higher-priority files and symlink changes invalidate the cache. Treat corrupt, obsolete and unavailable caches as misses, preserve real source diagnostics, and publish each cache entry atomically. Do not clone all typed bodies when encoding or consuming the shared snapshot.\n\nAcceptance: cold/warm and CLI execution tests, transitive/type-only edit and resolution invalidation, option/build mismatch and corrupted/partial cache recovery. Report frontend-cache timings separately from runtime/optimized HIR caching. Prelowered project HIR caching remains in the broader module issue and needs the existing snapshot compatibility fixes.\n\nParent: 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564","files":null}]}